{ This chapter will go over the Classical Variation, which is not as aggressive as the other variations of the Sicilian }
1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 Nc6 { This is the Old Sicilian } 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 d6 { This is the Classical Variation, which is not commonly used in the modern days } 6. Be3 g6 7. Qd2 Bg7 8. f3 O-O { [%cal Ge1b1,Gf1c4,Gg2g4] } 9. Bc4 (9. O-O-O Nxd4 10. Bxd4 Be6 { [%csl Ga2][%cal Ge6a2] } 11. Kb1 { [%csl Gc7,Gc8][%cal Gd8c7,Gf8c8] } 11... Qc7 12. h4 Rfc8) 9... Bd7 { [%cal Ga8c8,Gc8c1] } 10. O-O-O Rc8 { [%csl Gc4][%cal Gc8c1] } 11. Bb3 Ne5 12. Kb1 *


